        "original_id": "7c73bfa7-a9d0-547a-a804-0a696c1ca7c9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alfred L. Werker, Del Andrews, Erich von Stroheim, Boots Mallory, ZaSu Pitts, Jon Jost\n- Companies: Fox Film Corporation\n- Works: Ridin' the Wind, Hello, Sister!, Stolen Harmony\n- Roles: film director, independent filmmaker\n\nFacts:\n- Alfred L. Werker was born on December 2, 1896, and he worked in movies from 1917 through 1957 as a film director.\n- In 1925, Alfred L. Werker co-directed his first film, \"Ridin' the Wind,\" alongside director Del Andrews.\n- In 1933, Fox Film Corporation executives brought Alfred L. Werker in to re-shoot and re-edit Erich von Stroheim's film \"Hello, Sister!,\" which co-starred Boots Mallory and ZaSu Pitts.\n- Alfred L. Werker directed the film \"Stolen Harmony,\" whose climax features a car chase.\n- Jon Jost was born on 16 May 1943 in Chicago and is an American independent filmmaker.\n- Alfred L. Werker died on July 28, 1975.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "7bcb9302-551b-5c6d-8de0-db382ddcbe13",
        "text": "Page: Alfred L. Werker. Sentence: Alfred L. Werker (December 2, 1896 – July 28, 1975) was a film director whose work in movies spanned from 1917 through 1957.\nPage: Alfred L. Werker. Sentence: After a number of film production jobs and assistant directing, Werker co-directed his first film, \"Ridin' the Wind\" in 1925 alongside director Del Andrews.\nPage: Alfred L. Werker. Sentence: He was brought in by Fox Film Corporation executives to re-shoot and re-edit Erich von Stroheim's film \"Hello, Sister!\nPage: Alfred L. Werker. Sentence: \" (1933), co-starring Boots Mallory and ZaSu Pitts.\nPage: Jon Jost. Sentence: Jon Jost (born 16 May 1943 in Chicago) is an American independent filmmaker.\nPage: Stolen Harmony. Sentence: The movie climaxes with an exciting car chase and was directed by Alfred L. Werker.",
